    "TV diagnostic admits96/96/72/72/72 with8/7/6/5/4 events. Allfive observed conditional fractions are below10%, but these are reused-path, overlapping-fit descriptive results and cannot select or certify the architecture.",
    "TV17 admitted fits choose zero/.05/.10 on3/6/8 fits. Eight rejected fits fail the independent same-U B event criterion by one event; no additional beta/eta was introduced to rescue them.",
    "Within each TV automatic cohort, same-target B comparisons are8vs7,7vs7,6vs5,5vs5,4vs2. MeanG improves by0.000538–0.000924/year; meanMDD rises0.001988–0.003632; nominal fees fall0.210–0.262 perinitial100. This is a modest growth-cost-loss tradeoff, not risk dominance.",
    "Comparing TV to the old retained-set learner on common automatic paths lowers meanG and MDD in allfour nonempty repeats, while fees change sign across repeats. Different automatic cohorts must not be compared as full-population performance.",
    "Fourth-repeat annual service sees10/96 events; its full hypothetical B reference sees10/120. The rejected24 havezero hypothetical B events. This demonstrates a cohort-denominator effect, not a reason to tune a gate on outer outcomes or impute rejected-client returns.",
    "TV distance bounds the immediate fee of a hypothetical restoration, not its expected benefit. Both new architectures remain diagnostic controls and do not satisfy the final Q2 estimated-benefit-versus-cost decision requirement by themselves."
